  "summary": "DIR-083 complete - all five named migrations delivered on the certified DIR-082 primitives, plus the fix for a severe pre-existing crash found during recon. S1 COVER LETTERS: CRASH FIXED. The API returns FLAT cover rows (MySQLRepository.js:1068-1071 spreads the data JSON; routes/covers.js:18-19 returns them verbatim) but the old render dereferenced a nested item sub-object on every row, so the page threw a TypeError the moment the account held a single cover letter and only the empty account ever rendered - which is exactly why the reviewer only saw an empty-state wasteland. The render now reads the REAL fields (candidateFirstname / candidateLastname / title || jobTitle). The page mounts CubaPageFrame dense + CubaSplitView (left = selectable list with aria-current, right = LIVE Cover1 preview) + CubaHud + CubaToolbar. The preview consumes the FROZEN Cover1 template read-only through its real values contract, built by a new coverValues() helper. The HUD uses letterSignals() to compute Words, Paragraphs, Company named and Role named from the stored letter body - real derived values, and an empty body yields an empty HUD. A rejected read now becomes a visible error state with retry instead of an eternal spinner; the unused lottie spinner and its imports were removed. S2 JOB TRACKER: mounted in CubaPageFrame dense with a CubaHud bound to the EXISTING summarizePipeline(jobs) result (Tracked, Active, Submitted, Interview rate, Awaiting reply, Offers) - the same real object that already drives the board, so nothing is invented and an empty tracker renders no HUD. Each of the five stage columns gained min-h-0 plus md:max-h-[calc(100vh-var(--cuba-header-h)-16rem)] and md:overflow-y-auto cuba-scrollbar, so a long column scrolls internally instead of pushing the page down, while the reflowing 1/2/3/5 grid that guarantees no horizontal scrollbar is preserved. S3 SUBMITTED APPLICATIONS: mounted in CubaPageFrame dense with a CubaHud that replaces the four stat tiles, bound to the SAME real counts (appliedJobs.length, getStatusCount applied, getStatusCount interview, and the accepted/total success rate); the redundant stat block was removed so the header and HUD stay pinned while the list scrolls. S4 PORTFOLIOS: renderGridView() is now a modular Bento grid (data-testid portfolio-bento-grid) where the newest portfolio is the featured tile (sm:col-span-2 with a taller preview) and the rest flow into single modules (data-testid portfolio-bento-tile); a labelled starter-template strip (data-testid portfolio-template-strip, aria-labelledby) renders the REAL bundled preview assets with real alt text and routes into the builder create flow; and the whole file was swept from 51 legacy colour utilities to ZERO, including the grid card, the list view, the search and select controls and the delete dialog. S5 MESSAGES: the dual-pane chat is now locked to h-[calc(100vh-var(--cuba-header-h))] max-h-[...] overflow-hidden (data-testid messages-viewport-lock) with min-h-0 overflow-hidden on both panes, so each owns its internal scrollbar and the document never grows; the DIR-081 lg split and the mobile back-to-list control are preserved. S6 TESTS: new tests/dir083-candidate-page-migrations.test.mjs with 6 acceptance tests (AC1 the crash is fixed and the split view mounts, AC2 all five pages mount the certified primitives, AC3 all five files are legacy-utility free and Portfolios no longer uses max-w-7xl or bg-white, AC4 a11y landmarks and aria-current and labelled panes, AC5 the import allowlist proves no new dependency, AC6 no fabricated telemetry) and test:dir083 registered; the DIR-081 suite was updated in lockstep for the two legitimate supersessions. VERIFIED: dir083 6 passing, 118 passing across dir083 + dir082 + dir081 + dir080 + dir079 + dir048 + cuba-candidate-portal + cuba-design-system + copilot-command-surface, test:dir072..dir083 and test:design-system every script EXIT 0, test:product EXIT 0, security:static 67 passing, xampp-policy 4 passing, build EXIT 0 in 3.81s against a 4.0s budget, lint 0 errors, frozen cv-templates diff 0 with the Cover1 template consumed read-only. SCOPE NOTE: DIR-083 named exactly five migrations and all five are delivered; the wider DIR-082 backlog it did not name is unchanged and still ratcheted (DashboardSettings 1330, DashboardInterviews 764, DashboardHomepage 226, DashboardSupport 183, ResumesList 12) and no claim is made that those are complete. ZERO FABRICATION: no metric, row, latency or template name was invented."
